# A full dental visit, from finding the patient to treating the tooth.
# Ayesha (P-00001) starts with 3 teeth with issues; tooth 11 is healthy.

TEST "A full dental visit: find the patient, record a caries, then treat it"

GIVEN the demo data is fresh

# Find the patient
WHEN the dentist opens the patient list
THEN the dentist should see "12 patients"
WHEN the dentist searches for "Ayesha"
THEN the dentist should see "1 of 12 patients matches"
AND the dentist should see "Ayesha Rahman"
WHEN the dentist opens the record of "Ayesha Rahman"
THEN the dentist should see "ID P-00001"
AND the dentist should see "Penicillin allergy"

# Look at her teeth
WHEN the dentist opens the "Dental" tab
THEN 3 teeth should be listed with issues
AND the chart should show tooth 11 with "no active issues"

# Record a new problem on tooth 11
WHEN the dentist selects tooth 11
AND the dentist adds a "Caries" issue with "Moderate" severity
AND the dentist marks the "Occlusal (incisal)" surface
AND the dentist saves the issue
THEN the dentist should see "Issue added to tooth 11"
AND tooth 11 should show "Caries"
AND the chart should show tooth 11 with "Caries"
AND 4 teeth should be listed with issues
AND the page should have no accessibility problems

# Treat it
WHEN the dentist marks the "caries" issue as treated today
THEN tooth 11 should have no active issues
AND the chart should show tooth 11 with "no active issues"
AND 3 teeth should be listed with issues

# Everything is still there after a reload
WHEN the dentist reloads the page
THEN tooth 11 should have no active issues
AND 3 teeth should be listed with issues
AND the page should have no accessibility problems

END
